In the humid heart of Stranglethorn Vale, a sprightly Gnome Warlock named Zibber zipped along a muddy path, his purple robes snagging on thorny vines. At his side floated his mischievous Succubus, Lila, her wings flickering with impish delight. As they approached a bandit camp, Lila whispered, "Let me handle this," and with a wink, she cast Lesser Invisibility, wrapping Zibber in shadow. They slipped past the guards, but when things went awry, Zibber realized Lila’s crowd control was powerful, but when a patrol of trolls appeared, the Voidwalker’s Sacrifice shield would have saved him. Zibber sighed, recalling why most warlocks still summoned Voidwalkers: their survivability and taunt abilities made group content and PvP far less deadly, even if the Succubus was better for solo questing.

**Answer:** Voidwalkers provide essential survivability and threat management, making them more valuable in group situations and PvP, despite the Succubus’s utility for solo questing. [end of text]


